    <name>
      <text>ABRIDGED LIFE TABLES_q3(Maternity Hospital Capacity Analysis: Cots Needed and Average Stay )</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A maternity hospital delivers \({@newborn_per_week@}\) newborn babies per week, \({@p1@}\%\) of them leave the hospital within a week, \({@p2@}\%\) of the remaining one-week babies leave the hospital before they are two weeks old, \({@p3@}\%\) leave before they are three weeks old, \({@p4@}\%\) of the remaining before they are four weeks old and \({@p5@}\%\) of the remaining before they are five weeks old and the remainder before they are six weeks old. Use the information to answer the questions that follow:</p>
<p>
<strong style="color: blue;">Note:</strong>

<ol>
<li>
<p>Give your answer to the nearest whole number or correct to \(2\) decimal places where necessary.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>To calculate the values of \( l_x \) (the number of survivors to exact age \( x \)), you can follow these steps:</p>
<ul>
<li>For \( x = 0 \) (which corresponds to newborns at week \(0\)), let \( l_0 = {@l0@} \) newborn babies initially.</li>
<li>For each subsequent week (\( x = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 \)), you'll use the given survival rates to calculate the number of survivors.</li>
<li>For \( l_1 \) (number of babies at the end of week \(1\)) \(= {@l0@} \) (initial newborns) - \( {@p1@}\% \) of \( {@l0@} \) (those who leave within a week) = \(\displaystyle  {@l0@} - \frac{{@p1@}}{100} \times {@l0@} = {@l1@} \)</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><p>\({}_\text{n}\text{d}_\text{x}  = l_x – l_{x+n},\,  \displaystyle   {}_\text{n}\text{q}_\text{x}  =\frac{{}_\text{n}\text{d}_\text{x} }{l_x}\, , \text{L}_x = \frac{(l_x + l_{x+1})}{2}\, ,\text{T}_x=\sum_{i=0}^{n-1} \text{L}_{x+i},\) and \( \displaystyle e_{x}^{0}=\frac{\text{T}_x}{l_x}\)</p>
</li>
</ol>
